# EAS Build ignore rules for the Mindora mobile app.
#
# This lives at the REPO ROOT on purpose. Even though `eas build` runs from
# mobile/, EAS uploads the whole monorepo - the builder path is
# /home/expo/workingdir/build/mobile/android - so the ignore file it reads is
# the one at the archive root. A mobile/.easignore is never consulted.
#
# Three build failures came out of getting this wrong, in order:
#
# 1. With no .easignore, EAS falls back to .gitignore, whose `*.jar` rule
#    (correct for a Java monorepo) stripped
#    android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar from the upload while shipping
#    the rest of android/. Gradle had no wrapper to run:
#      Error: Unable to access jarfile .../android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
#    So there is deliberately NO `*.jar` rule here.
#
# 2. Putting the file in mobile/ changed nothing - android/ still arrived and
#    prebuild logged "Created native directory | reusing /android", reusing the
#    broken upload instead of generating a clean one.
#
# 3. Excluding everything via `/*` and re-admitting `!/mobile/` produced an
#    80-byte archive: EAS's matcher does not honour that re-include. Hence the
#    explicit list below rather than a whitelist - it is more verbose, but it
#    behaves predictably.

# --- Backend and web: irrelevant to an Android build, and most of the upload.
ai-service/
analytics-service/
auth-service/
common-library/
discovery-server/
file-service/
gateway-service/
journal-service/
notification-service/
python-ai-service/
recommendation-service/
search-service/
user-service/
frontend/
docs/
k8s/
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.githooks/

# --- Native projects are generated, not authored. Both are gitignored locally
# and rebuilt by prebuild; excluding them is what forces EAS to run a real
# prebuild, so the builder produces its own wrapper and cannot inherit ours.
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/

# --- Installed on the builder.
mobile/node_modules/

# --- Expo / Metro local state
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/web-build/
mobile/expo-env.d.ts
mobile/.metro-health-check*

# --- Local env: the production build takes its values from eas.json's `env`
# block, so uploading a local .env would only risk overriding them.
mobile/.env
mobile/.env*.local

# --- Play Store assets: needed for the listing, not for compiling the app.
mobile/play-assets/

# --- Signing material must never be uploaded.
mobile/*.jks
mobile/*.p8
mobile/*.p12
mobile/*.key
mobile/*.mobileprovision
mobile/*.pem

# --- Build outputs
mobile/*.apk
mobile/*.aab

# --- Misc
mobile/.kotlin/
mobile/*.orig.*
mobile/*.tsbuildinfo
mobile/npm-debug.*
mobile/yarn-debug.*
mobile/yarn-error.*
mobile/.DS_Store
